<header><p class="st-kicker">city state · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Commune of Vercelli</h1><p class="st-meta">1120 CE – 1335 CE (approx.) · capital Vercelli</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Piedmontese city-republic on the road to France that founded one of Italy's earliest universities in 1228.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Vercelli's powerful <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> held comital rights over the city, but citizens governed through consuls by around 1120. The commune expanded across the plain of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sesia">Sesia</a>, competing with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-novara">Novara</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casale-monferrato">Casale</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/march-of-montferrat">March of Montferrat</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/consul">Consuls</a> and later a podestà ran the commune, which joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-barbarossa">Frederick Barbarossa</a>. In 1228 it agreed with students and masters from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/commune-of-padua">Padua</a> to found a studium, one of the earliest Italian universities. Cardinal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guala-bicchieri">Guala Bicchieri</a>, papal legate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, founded the abbey of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basilica-of-santandrea-vercelli">Sant'Andrea</a>, a Gothic landmark begun in 1219. The rival Avogadro and Tizzoni families split the city.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1335 Vercelli accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/azzone-visconti">Azzone Visconti</a> and became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/lordship-of-milan">Lordship of Milan</a>. It passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-savoy">Duchy of Savoy</a> in 1427.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="city state, 1120 CE – 1335 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V42 H32 V34 H40 V42 H46 V34 H54 V42 H60 V34 H68 V42 H76 V82 Z"/><path d="M44 82 V66 Q50 58 56 66 V82"/><path d="M34 54 H40 M60 54 H66"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">city state</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Italy</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:81.99%;width:4.28%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1120 CE – 1335 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>city state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>mercantile</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Vercelli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Piedmontese, Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Vercelli</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1228&amp;focus=commune-of-vercelli" aria-label="Commune of Vercelli on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4880 578 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Commune of Vercelli lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5200 834L5218 830M5200 834L5140 827"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0M5140 827h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5200 834h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5200 834h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Vercelli. <a href="/atlas?year=1228&amp;focus=commune-of-vercelli">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
